  <data name="StoragePath_Error_Same" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} and {1} point to the same path ({2}). Both directories would read and write files with identical names and overwrite each other, so the setting was not saved. Choose two different folders.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="StoragePath_Error_Nested" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} ({1}) and {2} ({3}) are nested inside each other. Migrating data would process files recursively between them, which can fail or duplicate files, so the setting was not saved. Choose two folders that do not contain each other.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="StoragePath_Error_UnderAppDir" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} ({1}) is inside the application installation directory ({2}). App updates or uninstalls overwrite or delete files in that directory, which can cause data loss, so the setting was not saved. Choose a folder outside the application installation directory.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="StoragePath_Error_ParentOfAppDir" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} ({1}) is the parent directory of the application installation directory ({2}). It would contain the application's own files, mixing them with other content on the disk, so the setting was not saved. Choose a folder outside the application installation directory.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="StoragePath_Error_DriveRoot" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} ({1}) is a drive root. The application would create files directly in the drive, mixing them with other content on the disk, so the setting was not saved. Choose a subfolder of that drive.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="StoragePath_Error_Invalid" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} is not a valid folder path: {1} ({2}), so the setting was not saved. Select a folder that exists on a local disk.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="StoragePath_Error_SaveFailed" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The storage path setting could not be saved ({0}). Make sure the target folder exists and that the current account has write permission for it.</value>
  </data>
